.Dd October 7, 2026
.Dt BSDTHINKPAD-MUTE-LED 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bsdthinkpad-mute-led
.Nd turn a ThinkPad mute LED on or off
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm @LIBEXECDIR@/bsdthinkpad-mute-led
.Cm speaker | mic
.Cm 0 | 1
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility turns the speaker or microphone mute LED of a ThinkPad off
.Pq Cm 0
or on
.Pq Cm 1 .
It is the only part of
.Xr bsdthinkpad 1
that needs root, and it accepts nothing but these two forms.
.Bl -tag -width speaker
.It Cm speaker
Calls the ACPI method
.Dv SSMS
of the ThinkPad hotkey device with
.Xr acpi_call 8 .
The path of the device is taken from the sysctl
.Va dev.acpi_ibm.0.%location .
.Dv SSMS
also mutes
.Pq Cm 1
or unmutes
.Pq Cm 0
the speaker in hardware, so callers pass the state that
.Va dev.acpi_ibm.0.mute
already has.
.It Cm mic
Sets the sysctl
.Va dev.acpi_ibm.0.mic_led .
.El
.Pp
.Xr bsdthinkpad 1
and its panel plugin run
.Nm
through
.Xr pkexec 1 .
The polkit action
.Dq org.bsdthinkpad.mute-led
allows this without a password for the user at the console (the active
local session) and refuses it for remote and inactive sessions.
.Xr devd 8
runs it directly, through
.Pa @LIBEXECDIR@/bsdthinkpad-key ,
for the microphone mute key.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa @PREFIX@/share/polkit-1/actions/org.bsdthinkpad.mute-led.policy
the polkit action.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check whether the firmware has the method and try it, as root:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# acpidump -dt | grep "Method (SSMS"
# @LIBEXECDIR@/bsdthinkpad-mute-led speaker 1
# @LIBEXECDIR@/bsdthinkpad-mute-led speaker 0
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bsdthinkpad 1 ,
.Xr pkexec 1 ,
.Xr acpi_ibm 4 ,
.Xr acpi_call 8 ,
.Xr bsdthinkpad-setup 8 ,
.Xr devd 8
